      "writtenOn": "2017-05-22T21:39:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Still curious about how this works. barrier() is really a compiler barrier only, so the CPU is still free to reorder these writes. So could another CPU still see alloc-\u003evma being set before say alloc-\u003efree_async_space?",
      "parentUuid": "e1f4ffb8_6ea3da2c",
      "revId": "9e012b979ac0f6051e5b4ba855293c653476bcc4",
