      "writtenOn": "2017-06-15T17:21:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It doesn\u0027t, but I don\u0027t think this patch is where it should be fixed. This is just mirroring the proc-\u003epid / proc-\u003etsk fields which are set up in binder_open() -- so the fix is beyond the scope of this patch. The bug exists already in the upstream and common versions.\n\nHow about this:\n\n- in this patch, binder_open will pass \"tsk\" as a parameter to fill in these fields so we aren\u0027t repeating this in two places\n- since fixing this pid namespace bug is not really part of fine-grained-locking, we file a bug and I\u0027ll submit a patch on top of this patch set to fix it\n- I\u0027ll get that patch submitted here next week on top of Martijn\u0027s patches\n\nDoes that sound ok?",
